# USB: real-hardware testing on 2026-09-12 confirmed this kernel has NO
# legacy `/sys/class/android_usb/android0` node at all (`ls` on it fails
# outright), only the modern UDC gadget class (`/sys/class/udc/a600000.dwc3`
# exists and probes fine - the controller itself is not the problem).
# TWRP's own stock init.rc (bootable/recovery, not this device tree) already
# has a complete, correct ConfigFS gadget setup - mounts configfs, builds
# the full gadget tree, mounts the FunctionFS endpoints, and binds the UDC -
# entirely gated behind the `sys.usb.configfs` property. `getprop` on the
# device showed it defaulting to `0`, which is the entire reason nothing
# ever came up: every USB-bringup rule in stock init.rc requires
# `sys.usb.configfs=1` to fire at all. This was originally supposed to be
# set by this file's own (previously entirely commented-out) ConfigFS
# block; simply setting the property directly is enough to let TWRP's
# already-correct stock logic take over, without duplicating and possibly
# racing it. See docs/twrp-build-notes.md.

on init
    write /sys/class/backlight/panel0-backlight/brightness 200
    setprop sys.usb.configfs 1

on property:ro.boot.usbconfigfs=false
   setprop sys.usb.configfs 0

on property:ro.boot.recover_usb=*
    write /sys/bus/platform/devices/a600000.ssusb/mode "peripheral"

on property:ro.boot.usbcontroller=*
    setprop sys.usb.controller ${ro.boot.usbcontroller}

on fs
    wait /dev/block/platform/soc/${ro.boot.bootdevice}
    symlink /dev/block/platform/soc/${ro.boot.bootdevice} /dev/block/bootdevice

# Real-hardware testing on 2026-09-12 (this build) showed `sys.usb.config`
# ends up as "mtp,adb" by boot completion, not plain "adb" - something later
# in boot (likely TWRP's own MTP-enable logic) composes that combined value.
# The exact-match triggers in stock init.rc (`on property:sys.usb.config=adb`,
# which is what actually starts adbd at all) only match the literal string
# "adb", so with "mtp,adb" they silently never fire: adbd never starts,
# `sys.usb.ffs.ready` never becomes 1, and the gadget's UDC is never bound
# (all confirmed directly via a live TWRP terminal - UDC was empty,
# ffs.ready was 0). Setting this in `on boot` (late, after whatever sets
# "mtp,adb") rather than `on init` (early, easily overwritten) is what the
# actively-working ShionKanagawa gts7lwifi-twrp sibling build does too - an
# earlier attempt here moved this to `on init` during a simplification pass
# and likely broke exactly this. Forcing both the live and persisted
# property so nothing re-reads a stale "mtp,adb" back in.
on boot
    setprop persist.sys.usb.config adb
    setprop sys.usb.config adb
